    "q-118581": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118581",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $y=y(t),$ what is the carrying capacity of the following logistic growth model?\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=720y-8{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=5\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14157279/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8y(90-y),\\,y(0)=5.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=90.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $90.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
