    "q-353483": {
      "dom_id": "step-q353483",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "The download count $P(t)$ of a viral mobile game follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=4P(8\\,000-P),\\,P(0)=600.\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, measured in years. For which value of $P$ is the download count growing at the fastest possible rate?\n\n$P=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFor a logistic growth model, the fastest rate of growth occurs when $P=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14157279/assets/9019b26b417c757bbfab79afb39379c1fc7a892bc44e934c6f23c339deacfd68.png)\n\nFrom our equation, we see that $a=8000.$ Hence, the carrying capacity is $8000,$ and $P$ grows at its fastest possible rate when \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{1}{2}a=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8000=4000.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
